    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the \"permanent\" vs \"temporary\" distinction is what's killing me. if the board views the shed as a permanent encroachment, it's a much higher bar for the rezoning. are there any specific precedents or similar cases in municipal law where a temporary status was granted to a structure that's clearly been there for a while, just to allow for a rezoning to move forward?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
